    "lines": [
      {
        "scene": "hook",
        "text": "You think Apple only earns from iPhones? It doesn't. Here's why.",
        "start": 0.3,
        "seconds": 3.46,
        "window": 3.93,
        "fill": 0.88
      },
      {
        "scene": "promise",
        "text": "Google paid Apple $20B in one year, for one setting. Here's what it buys.",
        "start": 4.23,
        "seconds": 4.78,
        "window": 5.47,
        "fill": 0.874
      },
      {
        "scene": "which",
        "text": "That much money, for one setting? Which setting is worth it?",
        "start": 9.7,
        "seconds": 2.8,
        "window": 3.23,
        "fill": 0.867
      },
      {
        "scene": "searchbox",
        "text": "The search box. Type anything into Safari, the iPhone's browser, and Google answers first.",
        "start": 12.93,
        "seconds": 5.05,
        "window": 5.67,
        "fill": 0.891
      },
      {
        "scene": "free",
        "text": "But Google search is free. How does paying for it make sense?",
        "start": 18.6,
        "seconds": 3.04,
        "window": 3.5,
        "fill": 0.869
      },
      {
        "scene": "ads",
        "text": "Because every search shows ads, and a shop pays Google each time someone taps one.",
        "start": 22.1,
        "seconds": 4.33,
        "window": 5.0,
        "fill": 0.866
      },
      {
        "scene": "howmuch",
        "text": "So what does that one deal cost Google every day?",
        "start": 27.1,
        "seconds": 2.38,
        "window": 2.87,
        "fill": 0.829
      },
      {
        "scene": "perday",
        "text": "Spread over a year, that's $54.8M a day, and $2.3M every hour.",
        "start": 29.97,
        "seconds": 6.28,
        "window": 6.93,
        "fill": 0.906
      },
      {
        "scene": "turn",
        "text": "But here's the twist. It isn't a flat fee at all. Apple keeps 36% of the ad money Google makes from Safari searches.",
        "start": 36.9,
        "seconds": 7.32,
        "window": 7.97,
        "fill": 0.918
      },
      {
        "scene": "cut",
        "text": "So every time I search on my iPhone, Apple gets a cut?",
        "start": 44.87,
        "seconds": 3.07,
        "window": 3.5,
        "fill": 0.877
      },
      {
        "scene": "payoff",
        "text": "Every search that shows an ad. Google isn't paying for a setting. It's renting your habit, and the rent comes to $38,052 every minute.",
